-- An assert whose message carries a runtime value, for the host tests.
--
-- `assert(ok, 'what: ' .. detail)` builds its message before it checks, and
-- with -P nogc nothing frees that string: under SAN=asan every such assert
-- is a leak LeakSanitizer reports. check() builds the message only when it
-- fails. `detail` is anything `..` takes: a string or a number.
require 'string'

global function check(ok: boolean, msg: string, detail: auto): void
  if not ok then error(msg .. detail) end
end
